Tile properties backlayer
NPCBarrier keeps npcs off the farm
NoSpawn All to avoid debris/trees spawning
Buildable F to keep certain areas unbuildable like in front of patio

Set in tileset props
Diggable
Type Dirt

Tile properties pathslayer
Order sets where cabins go in multiplayer

Map properties
AllowGrassSurviveInWinter T/F
BackwoodsEntry tile player arrives on when entering from backwoods
BrookSounds see Audio in modding:maps
BusStopEntry see backwoods but bus stop
FarmCaveEntry see backwoods but farm cave
FarmHouseEntry tile you stand on when exiting the house; for typical 9x6, from the top left tile this will be at the fifth row down, sixth column to the right (in other words, take the coords of your top left tile, and add 5 to the first number and 4 to the second)
FarmHouseFlooring for starting farmhouse, see farmhouse interior in modding:maps
FarmHouseFurniture see above
FarmHouseStarterGift see above
FarmHouseStarterSeedsPosition see above
FarmHouseWallpaper see above
ForestEntry see backwoods but bus stop
GrandpaShrineLocation middle tile of the shrine, where the diamond goes
GreenhouseLocation top left corner tile of the greenhouse (gh is 7x6 tiles plus 3x2 at the front)
MailboxLocation base of mailbox default location - also needs to be patched, see modding:maps
Outdoors T
PetBowlLocation top left tile of 2x2 pet bowl
ShippingBinLocation top left tile of 2x2 shipping bin
SpouseAreaLocation top left tile of 4x4 patio
Warp for warps to bus stop/forest/backwoods/farm cave
WarpTotemEntry tile you stand on when arriving via warp totem

Icons for farm selection and world map

Fishing/Artifacts
Add via location data

Spawn monsters and grass on new year and wild/fruit trees

Spawn farm buildings and machines

Standard farmhouse size
Floor tiles are 1,4 to 10,10
Wall tiles are 1,1 to 10,3

For wallpaper count how many single-tile columns it is from start (don't forget index zero)
For flooring count how many double-tile columns it is from start (bc flooring is 2x2) (don't forget index zero)